{"author":{"id":"673e1e1b6fccff4da5524407c8a8cdc7caf18221aabb93f2bb36ffef5c2a95e8"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1781331242,"nonce":"4YnzbHNlO9HtUySvVumrdjhGC6o=","metadata":{"github-id":"I_kwDOSn4-Gc8AAAABFW8oFg","github-url":"https://github.com/kanya-approve/karpenter-provider-rackspace-spot/issues/13","origin":"github"},"title":"ServerClassSelector is declared in the CRD but never applied","message":"`RackspaceSpotNodeClassSpec.ServerClassSelector` is defined and documented as narrowing which ServerClasses are eligible, but nothing in the controller or cloudprovider ever reads it.\n\n### Evidence\n- Declared at `pkg/apis/v1/types.go:50-55` (`ServerClassSelector *metav1.LabelSelector`), doc comment: \"narrows which ServerClasses are considered when scheduling.\"\n- `grep -rn ServerClassSelector` matches **only** types.go. No reference in:\n  - `pkg/controllers/nodeclass/controller.go:83` `reconcileServerClasses` — calls `instanceType.List(region)` and maps **every** class name into `Status.ServerClasses`, unfiltered.\n  - `pkg/cloudprovider/cloudprovider.go:204` `GetInstanceTypes` — returns **all** region classes, unfiltered.\n\n### Impact\nA user who sets `serverClassSelector` to restrict provisioning (e.g. to cheaper or specific ServerClasses) is silently ignored; Karpenter may provision any ServerClass in the region. The CRD advertises a feature that is a no-op.\n\n### Suggested fix\n- Decide what labels a ServerClass exposes to match against (Name, Category, Resources-derived labels?) — needs a short design note, since `metav1.LabelSelector` matches label sets and Rackspace ServerClasses don't carry arbitrary labels today.\n- Apply the selector in both `reconcileServerClasses` (so Status reflects the eligible set) and `GetInstanceTypes` (so Karpenter only sees eligible types).\n- Unit-test selector match/no-match.\n\n### Acceptance\nSetting `serverClassSelector` measurably restricts `Status.ServerClasses` and the instance types offered to Karpenter.","files":null}]}